  "doc.access.opR4c": "Deletion cannot be undone; audit history keeps the name marked as deleted.",
  "doc.access.opR5a": "Copy Agent Prompt",
  "doc.access.opR5b": "Retrieves the secret and builds the full connection config.",
  "doc.access.opR5c": "Unavailable while the token is disabled; it is the only place in the UI that can hand the secret out again.",
  "doc.access.opTh1": "Action",
  "doc.access.opTh2": "Effect",
  "doc.access.opTh3": "Caveat",
  "doc.access.permP1": "Permissions come in two sections: database permissions decide which connections this token can see and query; tool permissions decide which MCP tools it can call. Both show an allowed over globally enabled count.",
  "doc.access.permP2": "When you turn a connection off, it disappears from that token's <code>datanexa_list_connections</code> result; calling it directly with the connection ID is rejected and recorded as a denial. When you turn a tool off, it disappears from <code>tools/list</code>, and direct calls are rejected the same way.",
  "doc.access.permR1a": "Databases",
  "doc.access.permR1b": "All allowed",
  "doc.access.permR1c": "Applies only to enabled connections; once off, the connection is invisible and unqueryable for this token.",
