  "doc.access.permR2b": "All allowed",
  "doc.access.permR2c": "Applies only to enabled tools; once off, the tool is not listed and cannot be called.",
  "doc.access.permR3a": "Global switches",
  "doc.access.permR3b": "Take precedence",
  "doc.access.permR3c": "If a connection or tool is disabled globally, the token switch is disabled and labeled Disabled globally; it cannot be enabled for one token alone.",
  "doc.access.permTh1": "Permission",
  "doc.access.permTh2": "Default",
  "doc.access.permTh3": "Notes",
  "doc.access.permTitle": "Permission granularity",
  "doc.access.preP1": "Access control depends on Bearer authentication. With Bearer on, a request is first mapped to a token, and that token's permissions filter databases and tools. With Bearer off, requests carry no identity and tokens cannot restrict anything.",
  "doc.access.preP2": "While Bearer is off, opening Access control shows a notice instead of the token list. Click Enable Bearer authentication in that notice; it updates the server config at the same time.",
  "doc.access.preTitle": "Prerequisite: enable Bearer first",
  "doc.access.preWarnText": "The token records are kept, but until Bearer is back on, any local program that can reach the endpoint needs no secret and is not limited by database or tool permissions. Do not hand out connection configs while it is off.",
  "doc.access.preWarnTitle": "Tokens stop applying once Bearer is off",
  "doc.access.rotateWarnText": "Rotation is immediate and has no grace period. Make sure you can edit the target client's config before you rotate, or that agent starts returning 401 right away.",
  "doc.access.rotateWarnTitle": "Have the replacement ready before rotating",
  "doc.access.secretP1": "The secret is never shown on the page. After creation or rotation it goes straight to the system clipboard; to get it again later, use Copy Agent Prompt for that token, which retrieves the secret and assembles the full config, again only into the clipboard.",
  "doc.access.secretP2": "So “the secret is shown only once” is not accurate: as long as you can copy the Agent Prompt, you can retrieve it. The real controls are disable, rotate and delete — all take effect immediately without restarting the service.",
